# Added in Phase 4A alongside `infra/docker/Dockerfile.migrations`, which is
# the first Dockerfile here to `COPY . .` -- every `services/<name>/Dockerfile`
# copies an explicit list of paths instead, so until now the build context's
# size only cost transfer time.
#
# Nothing listed below is copied by any existing Dockerfile (each names
# `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, and specific `packages/`/`services/`
# directories), so this cannot change what those images contain -- it only
# shrinks the context they transfer.

.git
.github

# Build outputs and caches
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.turbo
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# Local environment
.env
.env.local
**/.env.local
